---
/**
 * /upkeep/ — the monthly fee, published for the first time on 2026-09-11.
 *
 * WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS AT ALL. Upkeep was the only thing this practice sells whose
 * price appeared nowhere on the site. It had no page, and the two places that
 * mentioned it — /services/ and /main-street/ — said "Ongoing upkeep is optional,
 * on a retainer" in brackets and named no figure. D90 had raised it to what it is
 * now and called it the only line in the catalog that earns while the operator is
 * elsewhere, which made it the one product a visitor could not find and could not
 * price.
 *
 * THE FIGURE IS INTERPOLATED AND MUST STAY THAT WAY. scripts/check-dist.mjs carries
 * a rule refusing it hand-typed anywhere under src/pages, src/components or
 * src/data, with three controls proving the rule fires on a typed fee, stays quiet
 * on the same number as invented demo data, and stays quiet on upkeep wording
 * carrying a different figure. Never write the number into this file.
 *
 * AND ONE THING ABOUT THAT RULE IS WORTH KNOWING BEFORE TRUSTING IT. The
 * client-paper scanner in the same gate ALSO refuses this figure today, because
 * EXTRA_PAGE_USD happens to be the same number. So two rules cover this page and
 * only one of them is about upkeep. The day those figures stop matching, the
 * accidental cover disappears and the upkeep rule is the only thing left — which
 * is precisely why it was written rather than leaning on the coincidence.
 *
 * THE CAP RENDERS BESIDE THE FEE, NOT BELOW IT, and that placement is the decision
 * rather than the styling. rescueAudit.alsoSays sits the same way for the same
 * reason: under a figure a reader takes a limit for a disclaimer, beside it they
 * take it for what they are buying. An unbounded "small fixes as they arise" at
 * this fee is a worse deal for the practice than the same words at a third of it,
 * because what a buyer feels entitled to spend scales with what they paid.
 *
 * NO PAY BUTTON, for the reason /ai-fit/ and /advisory/ have none: this starts
 * after something has been built, so it begins in a conversation rather than at a
 * checkout.
 *
 * THE PAGE SAYS STOPPING IT TURNS NOTHING OFF, and that sentence is load-bearing
 * rather than reassurance. D37's whole delivery model is a hosted copy in the
 * client's own account plus an offline file they keep, so a canceled retainer
 * disables nothing. A monthly fee on a site that promises "no subscription, no
 * lock-in" has to answer that out loud or the two read as a contradiction.
 */
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { upkeep } from '../data/services';
import { Wrench, Timer, ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';

const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    '@id': `${origin}/upkeep/#service`,
    name: 'Monthly upkeep',
    serviceType: 'Software maintenance',
    provider: { '@id': `${origin}/#business` },
    description:
      'An optional monthly arrangement for software already delivered: small fixes and changes as they arise, with a stated limit, cancellable at any time.',
  },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Keeping it running, after it is built"
  description={`An optional monthly arrangement for what I have already built you — small fixes and changes as they arise, with a stated limit. ${upkeep.amount}`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-14">
      <p class="mono-label">Optional · after the build · stop whenever you like</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Keeping it running, after it is built.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        {upkeep.whoItIsFor}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Nothing about a build needs this. What was made for you is yours outright and it keeps
        working whether or not you ever send me another message. This is for the version of you who
        would rather not be the one editing it.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
        <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-2 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{upkeep.line}</p>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{upkeep.qualifier}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* THE REFUSAL RENDERS BESIDE THE FIGURE. See the header: beside it this
          reads as the terms, below it as a disclaimer, and it is the half that
          makes the fee honest rather than open-ended. */}
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{upkeep.alsoSays}</p>

      <ul class="mt-7 grid max-w-3xl gap-2">
        {upkeep.includes.map((item) => (
          <li class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">— {item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact/?intent=consult">
          Ask about it <ArrowUpRight class="size-4" />
        </a>
        <a class="link-sweep text-sm" href="/services/">Or see what I build first →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-3 p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Timer class="size-5 text-accent" />
          <span class="mono-label">The limit</span>
        </div>
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">
          {upkeep.minutes} minutes a month, and it says so here.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{upkeep.cap}</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
          A monthly fee with no stated limit is one of us guessing and the other hoping. Written
          down, neither of us has to have that conversation in month four.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-3 p-7">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <Wrench class="size-5 text-secondary" />
          <span class="mono-label">What it is not</span>
        </div>
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">
          Not a license, and not a condition of anything.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          This buys my time, not permission to keep using what you own. Stop it and nothing is
          switched off, nothing degrades, and nothing phones home — what was built sits in your own
          accounts with a copy you keep offline.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
          That is why this sits on its own page rather than inside a build price. A thing you can
          decline is a thing that has to be described honestly enough to decline.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
